      "role": "user",
      "content": "wow okay lol. \"tinfoil hat\" argument? that's a bit harsh, don't you think? my professors are pretty old school and they'd probably say that dismissing the need for confidential advice as a \"tinfoil hat\" thing is pretty bad legal scholarship. \n\nif the privilege is the only thing keeping the executive branch functional and preventing the legislature from turning into a grand jury that micromanages every single move the president makes, isn't that a very real constitutional crisis? are you saying the oversight argument is just objectively better because of some moral high ground?",
